{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473238-vampires-cry-blood-a-bit-of-sillyness","id":1473238,"title":"Vampires cry blood: a bit of sillyness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-25T00:11:11-08:00","id":1473238,"title":"Vampires cry blood: a bit of sillyness?","content":"Vampires should, normally, cry regular tears, be capable of sweating regular-seeming sweat, and create sexual fluids that aren't the height of embarrassment. Why? &quot;you cry blood&quot; always seems be said in a tone that reminds me of a 14 year old thinking he knows what's cool. It's not cool. It's lame. It's really really lame. It might be great for a specific scene, but it's something that really suffers with overuse. (also note: Vampire magic being excessively blood themed. Juvenile.) <br /> <br /> 1: Why not? Because a vampire cried blood in a movie and it looked cool? Well, Can't-cross running water and fear of crosses were features of movies, and they're regulated to a flaw in VTM. All of a vampire's fluids are replaced by blood? Rediculous. Vampires would have eyes literally filled with blood if that were the case, and Vampire saliva is, in VTM, not Vitae but a separate fluid. <br /> 1: Because they're skillfull deceptors. If you can't cry without freaking people out, what good are you at deception? A Casanovva's entire feeding strat revolves around getting kine in the bedroom; You're a Virgin &quot;every time&quot; or on your period every single night doesn't work. <br /> <br /> Blood sweat exists IRL, only it's something not so noticeable. The sweat is slightly tinged red, it's not exactly horror show stuff. Crying blood... sure, it exists, But does that mean that decent-humanity vampires using the blush of life need to have it? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T01:56:57-08:00","id":1473241,"title":"","content":"And? If you want to get rid of it in your games, nobody's gonna stop you here.<br /> <br /> But the logic is crap and you know it, because you could apply it to <b>any</b> pop culture vampire tropes, and VtM is literally build on a mix of oldish Gothic vampires tropes and newer 70s-80s vampire tropes. There is no basic element of the game that you can't make a claim to be silly or &quot;lame&quot; especially due to overuse/overexposure in pop culture, and thus should be cut. If you cut all that out, you would be left it a mediocre system with no purpose to it and a giant vampire-ish shaped hole in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T05:27:48-08:00","id":1473250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473238-vampires-cry-blood-a-bit-of-sillyness#post1473238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires should, normally, cry regular tears, be capable of sweating regular-seeming sweat, and create sexual fluids that aren't the height of embarrassment. Why? &quot;you cry blood&quot; always seems be said in a tone that reminds me of a 14 year old thinking he knows what's cool. It's not cool. It's lame. It's really really lame. It might be great for a specific scene, but it's something that really suffers with overuse. (also note: Vampire magic being excessively blood themed. Juvenile.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it is silly, especially if you consider how <b>ridiculously easy </b>would be to detect a Vampire if it was the case. Every time you kiss someone you have to explain the taste of blood. It's a good thing it is no longer a thing if you Blush, as your blood transforms to mimic other fluids, in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Casanovva's entire feeding strat revolves around getting kine in the bedroom; You're a Virgin &quot;every time&quot; or on your period every single night doesn't work. </div> </div> </div>Even with...blood fluids, feeding during kissing (if you ignore that your kisses would taste like blood, or do some other thing to mask the taste), is probably quicker, more practical and safe for the Masquerade than having actual sex anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T06:31:51-08:00","id":1473254,"title":"","content":"More than a bit. Vampire, uh, biology is all silly and all of it collapses in my eyes the moment I start looking at it. Vampires can extract water and such from blood well enough to produce saliva and occular fluid, but not for sweat or tears. Ok. Kindred physicality as written is designed for aesthetic, because magic.<br /> <br /> Ridiculous as crying blood is, I can at least understand it from a drama/aesthetic perspective. And crying is a moment of pain and vulnerability, a theme of vulnerability enhanced by the fact that it's possibly going to make other vampires around you into an immediate physical danger. Silly, but it has a theme. Meanwhile' <i>Sweat??</i><br /> <br /> The bit about vampires sweating blood that gets me most is the fact that they <i>sweat</i>. What... what purpose does that even serve? The majority of the vampire's host's internal organs are left to atrophy, because it has no need for them, but it instinctually maintains its sweat glands? Because...? To maintain its nonexistent body temperature to protect the function of dead organs? With a liquid that can't perform the function of sweat and encourages its fellow vampires to cannibalise it by its scent? A being that has to consciously remember to practice breathing and blinking because those basic behaviours aren't instinctive camoflauge to it can sweat and waste vitae for zero purpose whatseover. <i>What.</i> (On reflection, I suppose it's another vulnerability relating to stress and fear. Nevetheless, I stand by my initial opinion; <i>what</i>.<i>)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 01-25-2022, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T06:39:11-08:00","id":1473255,"title":"","content":"I go with normal body fluids can be created for a prize. Blood is only used in case of roll failure or for dramatic effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26030-mfalkenb","name":"mfalkenb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T07:22:59-08:00","id":1473260,"title":"","content":"I think the thing is that whoever first wrote down that idea was really cool, but it's become a way over used meme since then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T20:15:48-08:00","id":1473309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mfalkenb</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473238-vampires-cry-blood-a-bit-of-sillyness?p=1473255#post1473255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go with normal body fluids can be created for a prize. Blood is only used in case of roll failure or for dramatic effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really great idea<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T21:08:31-08:00","id":1473379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473238-vampires-cry-blood-a-bit-of-sillyness#post1473238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">said in a tone that reminds me of a 14 year old thinking he knows what's cool. It's not cool. It's lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you...have you consumed any piece of Vampire media since the inception of the rpg?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T21:56:10-08:00","id":1473381,"title":"","content":"Normal human excretions should be a function of Humanity. The higher humanity, the more likely you can do things like cry or even sweat. Humanity 10 should be almost indistinguishable from being alive - but who has Humanity 10?. Humanity 7 should allow a vampire to fake it under normal circumstances, but there should be some effort involved. Under that and things begin to not work properly because it's more and more obvious you are a corpse.<br /> <br /> Things like crying blood should only be done for flavor text purposes, and thus used sparingly. Your level of tolerance for it is a matter of taste. What one person thinks as being silly is another's definition of cool. I'm not big on policing someone else's taste, though it could certainly cause me to decline playing in someone's game. It's OK if I think someone else's game is not cool, and vice versa. At a certain point, you need to determine different tastes are OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T05:06:52-08:00","id":1473394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473238-vampires-cry-blood-a-bit-of-sillyness?p=1473381#post1473381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal human excretions should be a function of Humanity. The higher humanity, the more likely you can do things like cry or even sweat. Humanity 10 should be almost indistinguishable from being alive - but who has Humanity 10?. Humanity 7 should allow a vampire to fake it under normal circumstances, but there should be some effort involved. Under that and things begin to not work properly because it's more and more obvious you are a corpse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make the other fluids a function of Blush of Health (which is free if your Humanity is 8+, but progressively more expensive as it drops barring the merit or excessively high generation). No additional rules needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T12:47:39-08:00","id":1473419,"title":"","content":"Yep. That blood point spend was what I was thinking of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}